WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.250
- Okay so everyone on the internet is arguing about IMHO.

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:06.050
^- Your social media users are in a heated debate

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.570
^over the internet acronym IMHO.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.970
- This started with the folks at Buzzfeed

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:15.030
who got into a heated debate over the abbreviation IMHO.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.130
^- And obviously it's--

00:00:17.337 --> 00:00:18.800
- Your opinion is obviously honest

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.090
why would you have to clarify that?

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:21.630
- I've never read it as "humble".

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.450
- Today we're gonna get to the bottom of this.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.600
- I'm gonna talk to the experts.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.790
- And I'm gonna talk to the people.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.623
Let's go.

00:00:26.887 --> 00:00:29.220
(pop music)

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.500
- So we have to find Lauren

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.150
because she's the one who wrote the article

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.283
that started this entire debate.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.923
I gotta ask you about IMHO.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.633
What happened?

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.000
^- Yes, I mean thank you. You're welcome.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.247
My friend Morgan said something and I responded, "IMHO"

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.820
and she goes "I don't know what you're saying."

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.507
Then as soon as I said "In my honest opinion,"

00:00:51.636 --> 00:00:55.050
I was getting attacked left and right.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.050
My coworkers were like, "In my honest opinion?

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.680
^Do you mean 'In my humble opinion?'"

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.790
^We've had this huge miscommunication for years

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:01.960
^I don't know you at all.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.220
^- If you say, "In my honest opinion I like your shirt."

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.640
- To me I'm like take it or leave it;

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:11.417
in my humble opinion you should cut this joke.

00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:13.180
- "In my humble opinion" makes you sound like

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:14.930
you're a prospector from the 1840s.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.696
(mimicking 1840s voice) "In my humble opinion".

00:01:17.696 --> 00:01:20.133
- Well there's something humorously.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.720
- [Lauren] The room was divided, it was bloody.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.510
I'm like this is kind of interesting,

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.773
let's put it to the masses of the internet.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:27.683
See what they have to say.

00:01:27.683 --> 00:01:29.913
The majority of the people; the popular vote,

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:31.500
were with "honest".

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.900
I'm not just giving you my opinion,

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.833
I'm giving you my honest opinion!

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:36.760
I'm not gonna sit here and lie to you.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.140
Those who think it's humble,

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.740
they just couldn't really face the fact

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:40.750
that they were losing.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.577
Their argument is that there's the phrase

00:01:42.577 --> 00:01:43.730
"in my humble opinion,"

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:44.563
which I know.

00:01:44.563 --> 00:01:48.330
But nobody says that really anymore.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.580
There was a clear winner.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.240
And it was "honest."

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.450
- Lauren's obviously team "honest"

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:55.080
but we're gonna get a second opinion.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.250
I talked to the Buzzfeed news Copy Chief and she said--

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.100
^- In my humble opinion.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.257
^Is that 100% on that? Or--

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.665
^- I would say it's 100%.

00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:04.750
(whooping)
- Okay, no.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:07.270
- That's it! It's humble! That's the answer!

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.310
I was right from the beginning.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.670
- Most of the dictionaries that we looked at

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:11.190
are house dictionaries, Merriam Webster,

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.590
and they're on team "humble."

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:14.890
On Youznet which is basically like Reddit

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:15.930
before there was Reddit,

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.580
came out of a longer acronym;

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.110
In My Not So Humble Opinion

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.730
and it was used pretty sarcastically.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.280
So the general consensus there was "humble"

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.860
and there are many more instances

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:28.270
of "in my humble opinion" than "in my honest opinion."

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:30.860
- When we tweeted the question most people said "honest."

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:31.980
- What that's indicative of

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.050
is sort of a generational divide.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.190
Older people are saying humble

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.210
and younger people are saying honest.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.840
- So is it possible that the younger people could win

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.090
just because old people will die before them?

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.003
- Yes.

00:02:44.003 --> 00:02:45.040
The one thing we can all agree on

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.070
is that the English language is a god damn mess.

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:49.823
- Okay Eric what did the people say?

00:02:49.823 --> 00:02:51.580
- The people said. First of all

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.430
I just want to say the people don't know anything

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:54.670
and they're not smart.
- That's not true.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:56.260
^- So we're going NYU campus

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.430
^because I feel like the kids there probably have the answer.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:00.300
^They're educated. They take English classes.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.760
Okay they're people but they haven't studied language.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.090
Most people at NYU said that it was "honest."

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:06.690
What does "IMHO" mean?

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:07.710
- In my honest opinion.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:08.543
- Why?

00:03:08.543 --> 00:03:09.376
- Honest?

00:03:09.376 --> 00:03:11.310
Because I always think you're being humble

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.260
if it's just in your opinion.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.200
- No but I always think you're being honest.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.200
If you're giving an opinion you're gonna be honest.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.350
- No I've given opinions that I have not believed in.

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:20.200
Devil's advocate.

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:21.103
- Whatever!

00:03:21.103 --> 00:03:22.557
- Honest would make more sense I think.

00:03:22.557 --> 00:03:23.390
- Honest, yeah.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:24.223
- Why?

00:03:24.223 --> 00:03:25.056
- I don't think our generation

00:03:25.056 --> 00:03:26.680
uses the word humble anymore unless

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.766
it's talking about Kendrick's song,

00:03:29.766 --> 00:03:31.610
like sit down be humble?

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.973
I mean I don't know.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:34.011
- Humble or honest?

00:03:34.011 --> 00:03:36.094
(groans)

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:38.800
- What'd you say?

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.140
- Is it "in my honest opinion?"

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.387
or "humble opinion"?

00:03:42.351 --> 00:03:43.184
- I don't know.

00:03:43.184 --> 00:03:44.043
- Humble or honest?

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:47.370
Well you got it here today,

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.340
it means...

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:49.863
- In my honest opinion.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.900
- I don't understand why everybody thinks it's honest.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.390
- It flows better off the tongue,

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.690
in my honest opinion or in my humble opinion

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.520
I would much rather hear "honest opinion".

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.880
- Watch when I asked the older generation

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:03.797
who's wiser and smarter, they said "humble".

00:04:03.797 --> 00:04:05.010
- "In my humble opinion."

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:05.843
- Finally! Why?

00:04:05.843 --> 00:04:07.163
- It's what my dad always said.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.053
- [Together] Humble.

00:04:08.053 --> 00:04:10.140
- These two right here have said there's no debate

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.020
it's 100% humble.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.220
- We're old school, man.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:14.690
- Thank you for solving the problem.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.633
Thank you guys.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:16.620
Yeah, more people said honest--

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.320
- So in a democracy it's honest.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.570
- I asked more younger people than I did older people.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.790
- It doesn't matter because I talked to a linguist

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:23.860
from Columbia.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.860
This is an Ivy League school

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.820
where people know what they're talking about.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:31.140
And she's gonna settle the IMHO debate once and for all.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:31.973
Right Michelle?

00:04:31.973 --> 00:04:32.806
- Absolutely.

00:04:32.806 --> 00:04:35.007
^"In my humble opinion," is more like lots of love.

00:04:35.007 --> 00:04:38.683
^"In my honest opinion," is more like laughing out loud.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.000
^- 80 years ago people would sign their letters

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:43.167
"LOL; lots of love."

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:44.940
Language changes.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:48.293
- My mom always texts me LOL when I text her goodnight.

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:49.708
- So she's not laughing at me?

00:04:49.708 --> 00:04:50.900
- No she's not laughing at you.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:52.490
- I thought she was just always laughing at me.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:53.737
- You're saying you think

00:04:53.737 --> 00:04:56.307
"in my honest opinion" is correct.

00:04:56.307 --> 00:04:58.500
- I'm not gonna say it's correct.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.510
It is far more commonly used by younger people

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:03.470
than by older people.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.470
It is the new and emergent

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:08.527
and evolving way to say "IMHO".

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.017
But really what you wanna say is "IMHO".

00:05:11.096 --> 00:05:12.767
"IMHO" doesn't really mean

00:05:12.767 --> 00:05:14.060
"In my humble opinion"

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:15.410
or "in my honest opinion"

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.683
it means "I am going to tell you my opinion,

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:20.160
whether or not it's appropriate for me to do so or not

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:21.900
but I'm just gonna put my opinion out there."

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.833
- It's hedging your strong opinion.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.333
It has its own meaning.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:26.710
Everyone's wrong.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.910
- So the honest and the humble don't matter?

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:29.883
- Not really.

00:05:29.883 --> 00:05:32.120
- Why has there never been a definitive decision though?

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.820
- Merriam Webster and Oxford,
- Oh Merriam Webster...

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.150
they both say humble.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:37.940
- I would love to know the average age

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.800
of the lexicographers in the world.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.853
I would guess it's probably over 25.

00:05:42.047 --> 00:05:44.480
I'm not gonna say they're too old to really know.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.610
- Okay I'll say they're too old to really know.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.040
You can't trust them.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:51.440
Who is the final arbiter of what is the correct definition?

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:56.060
- 100% of 18 to 21 year olds have a cell phone.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:58.380
If 100% of the young people

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.480
are communicating in this language variety

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.493
they're gonna win.

00:06:01.493 --> 00:06:03.650
- IMHO is basically just going through puberty.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:05.760
- It is definitely going through puberty.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:06.593
- So that's the answer.

00:06:06.593 --> 00:06:07.426
- IMHO

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:09.943
means something beyond honest or humble.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.320
Let's stop talking about it.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.153
We ended it.

00:06:12.153 --> 00:06:13.000
- It's over!

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.230
- Let us know your honest--
- No!

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:16.070
- Or humble opinions.
- No!

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:17.700
because we just told them it's over!

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:19.550
Don't let us know your honest or humble opinions.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:20.780
- Okay and the comments!

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.510
- Don't you dare comment your opinion on this video

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:25.570
- Whether it be honest or humble,

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.760
- Yeah it's over.
- We don't wanna hear it.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:28.920
- We already figured it out.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.720
- We figured it out. You're welcome.

